---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../../components/editorial/SectionLabel.astro';
import MediaFrame from '../../components/editorial/MediaFrame.astro';
import OperatingDiagram from '../../components/editorial/OperatingDiagram.astro';
import { media } from '../../data/media';
import { mediaManifest } from '../../data/site';
---

<Layout title="Employee experience for EoR teams | Trustora" description="Trustora connects the EoR employee journey across offer, onboarding, pay, benefits, support, development, mobility, and offboarding." currentPath="/employee-experience/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="measure page-hero-grid"><div class="page-hero-copy"><SectionLabel>Employee experience</SectionLabel><h1>Make the employment relationship legible.</h1><p>EoR is not a background vendor relationship. It is part of what the employee feels when the offer arrives, the first payment lands, a question appears, or the work changes.</p></div><div class="page-hero-media"><MediaFrame src={media['accessible-remote-call']} alt={mediaManifest['accessible-remote-call'].alt} caption="Clarity in pay and benefits is one of the most tangible forms of trust in an employment relationship." credit={mediaManifest['accessible-remote-call'].credit} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 38vw" priority /></div></div></section>
  <section class="section cream-field"><div class="measure"><div class="section-head"><div><SectionLabel>The employee journey</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">One relationship. Many moments.</h2></div><p>Trustora helps keep the handoffs visible across the employment lifecycle.</p></div><div class="process-map"><div class="process-step"><span>01</span><h3>Offer & contract</h3><p>Make the employing model and local context understandable.</p></div><div class="process-step"><span>02</span><h3>Day one</h3><p>Join documents, equipment, access, manager context, and belonging.</p></div><div class="process-step"><span>03</span><h3>Pay & benefits</h3><p>Give people a dependable rhythm and a human route to answers.</p></div><div class="process-step"><span>04</span><h3>Growth & change</h3><p>Support development, mobility, workplace change, and offboarding.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section cream-field"><div class="measure"><div class="section-head"><div><SectionLabel>Experience architecture</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">The handoffs are the experience.</h2></div><p>When the sequence is visible, the employee does not have to carry the complexity alone.</p></div><OperatingDiagram kind="journey" label="Employee experience journey from offer to support and growth" /></div></section>
  <section class="section blue-field"><div class="measure story-grid"><div class="story-copy"><SectionLabel>Employee intelligence</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">Context about the work. Never surveillance of the person.</h2><p>Our view is that employee intelligence means understanding the conditions around specialist work: the capability, the role, the team, the country, the workplace, and the decisions that need a clear owner.</p><p>It should not mean keystroke monitoring, demographic inference, or presence metrics disguised as contribution.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/insights/eor-with-employee-intelligence/">Read the point of view <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><MediaFrame src={media['dry-lab-data-review']} alt={mediaManifest['dry-lab-data-review'].alt} caption="Specialist teams are built from expertise, context, and the conditions that let people do difficult work well." credit={mediaManifest['dry-lab-data-review'].credit} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 55vw" /></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="measure split-argument"><div><SectionLabel>Support in practice</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">The right answer has an owner.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>When a person has a question about pay, leave, benefits, employment documents, equipment, working location, or a change to the relationship, the route should not be a maze.</p><p>We map what Trustora coordinates, what the client company owns, and where qualified country specialists need to advise. Clear boundaries make human support more credible.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/insights/the-trust-layer-in-global-employment/">Read about the trust layer <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section cream-field"><div class="measure"><div class="section-head"><div><SectionLabel>Employee experience library</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">Build the journey before the first day.</h2></div></div><div class="capability-links"><a href="/insights/eor-employee-experience/"><span>01</span><strong>EoR as an operating system</strong><small>Five layers people actually feel.</small></a><a href="/insights/onboarding-across-borders/"><span>02</span><strong>Onboarding across borders</strong><small>Make the first ten days credible.</small></a><a href="/services/benefits-administration/"><span>03</span><strong>Benefits administration</strong><small>Explain local choices and support.</small></a><a href="/employee-experience-brief/"><span>04</span><strong>Employee experience brief</strong><small>Access the working material.</small></a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section dark-field"><div class="measure intro-slab"><div><SectionLabel light>Design the relationship</SectionLabel><h2 class="mt-2">Make the employee feel the operating model working.</h2></div><div class="intro-body"><p>Bring us the role, country, employee journey, and open questions. We will help turn them into an accountable sequence.</p><a class="button button-light" href="/employee-experience-brief/">Request the experience brief <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
</Layout>
